  "narrative": "The independent review of the DailySpend trial (austin-org, org/org-development/process-study/trial-review-2026-11-04.md) found what the tool cost the session: no re-parent (T1), two numbering schemes (T2), a flat top level with nothing to say about a childless root (T3), \"technical\" on a person's requirement (T4), no append (T5), hidden done children with no marker (T6), amend refusing a leaf (T7), mixed separators (T8), plus the session's own asks: a one-level view, colour, and seeing one's own started work. Each child is one of those; the last child is the release itself, carrying the release type.\n\nAmended 2026-11-04T21:58:29Z: The adopt event kind and the task's former positions are the first change to what the store writes since 0.4.2, so the rule settled 2026-11-03 (P5) applies: a format line in .tasks/config, written by init and the first write of a newer binary; a binary meeting a newer format refuses with one sentence."
